---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import { categories, sourceUrl, sourceUpdated, liveChecked } from '../../data/rbac-permissions';
import { fmtDate } from '../../lib/content';

const topic = await getEntry('topics', 'rbac');
const slug = (s: string) => s.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/(^-|-$)/g, '');
const total = categories.reduce((n, c) => n + c.perms.length, 0);
const never = categories
  .map((c) => ({ c, perms: c.perms.filter((p) => p.tier === 'never') }))
  .filter((x) => x.perms.length);
const neverCount = never.reduce((n, x) => n + x.perms.length, 0);
const updated = fmtDate(new Date(sourceUpdated), { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' });
const checked = fmtDate(new Date(liveChecked), { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' });
const liveCount = categories.reduce((n, c) => n + c.perms.filter((p) => p.live).length, 0);
const title = 'Intune RBAC permission reference';
const description = `Every permission you can put in an Intune custom role: Microsoft's description, what it really lets someone do, and the ones I'd never grant by default.`;
---
<Base title={title} description={description} accent={topic?.data.accent} accentDark={topic?.data.accentDark}>
  <header class="head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/rbac/">Intune RBAC</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Reference</span></nav>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Every permission you can put in an Intune custom role, with Microsoft's description and, where it helps,
        what the permission really lets someone do. Plus the ones I'd never grant by default.
      </p>
      <p class="facts">{categories.length} categories · {total} permissions · Source: <a href={sourceUrl}>Microsoft Learn</a> (updated {updated}), checked against a live tenant on {checked}</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap body">
    <section class="intro prose">
      <h2>How to read this</h2>
      <p>
        Each permission is a <strong>category</strong> plus an <strong>action</strong>, exactly as they appear when you build a custom role
        in <strong>Tenant administration › Roles › All roles › Create</strong>. For each one you'll see:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Microsoft's description,</strong> word for word from Microsoft Learn.</li>
        <li>
          <span class="badge new">New</span> marks the {liveCount} permissions that exist in a live tenant but aren't on Microsoft Learn yet.
          Their description is the one Intune itself returns through Microsoft Graph.
        </li>
        <li><strong>In practice:</strong> my note on what the action actually touches and what can go wrong. I added these wherever Microsoft's description just repeats the action name, or where the impact isn't obvious.</li>
        <li>
          A rating: <span class="badge never">Never by default</span> means grant only to a small, named group, ideally just-in-time.
          <span class="badge high">High impact</span> means it changes devices or users at scale, or exposes sensitive data, so grant it deliberately and scope it tightly.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The ratings are my recommendations from years of working with Intune customers. They aren't Microsoft guidance.
        For how categories and actions combine into roles, start with <a href="/rbac/day-05/">Day 5: Anatomy of a permission</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="never-box" aria-labelledby="never-h">
      <h2 id="never-h">The {neverCount} permissions I'd never grant by default</h2>
      <p>These destroy data, hand over keys and passwords, open remote access with no one watching, or control RBAC itself.</p>
      <ul class="never-list">
        {never.map(({ c, perms }) => (
          <li><span class="nc">{c.name}</span>{perms.map((p) => <a href={`#${slug(c.name)}--${slug(p.action)}`}>{p.action.replace(/\.$/, '')}</a>)}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="check prose" aria-labelledby="check-h">
      <h2 id="check-h">Check the list against your tenant</h2>
      <p>
        Intune adds permissions as features ship, and documentation can lag behind. When I last checked, a live tenant had five permissions that weren't documented yet. To see exactly what's live in yours,
        run this in <a href="https://aka.ms/ge">Graph Explorer</a> (it needs <code>DeviceManagementRBAC.Read.All</code>):
      </p>
      <pre><code>GET https://graph.microsoft.com/beta/deviceManagement/resourceOperations?$select=resourceName,actionName,description</code></pre>
      <p>Or with the Microsoft Graph PowerShell SDK, following every page of results:</p>
      <pre><code>{`Connect-MgGraph -Scopes DeviceManagementRBAC.Read.All
$uri = 'https://graph.microsoft.com/beta/deviceManagement/resourceOperations?$select=resourceName,actionName,description'
$ops = while ($uri) {
    $page = Invoke-MgGraphRequest -Uri $uri
    $page.value
    $uri = $page.'@odata.nextLink'
}
$ops | Sort-Object resourceName, actionName |
    Select-Object resourceName, actionName, description |
    Export-Csv .\\intune-permissions.csv -NoTypeInformation`}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <div class="tools" role="search">
      <label for="q">Filter permissions</label>
      <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="Try wipe, assign, key, password…" autocomplete="off" />
      <label class="chk"><input id="risky" type="checkbox" /> Only high impact and never by default</label>
      <p id="count" class="count" aria-live="polite">{total} permissions</p>
    </div>

    <nav class="index" aria-label="Categories">
      {categories.map((c) => <a href={`#${slug(c.name)}`} data-cat-link={slug(c.name)}>{c.name}</a>)}
    </nav>

    <div id="ref">
      {categories.map((c) => (
        <section class="cat" id={slug(c.name)} data-cat={slug(c.name)}>
          <h2>{c.name}</h2>
          <p class="sum">{c.summary}</p>
          <ul class="perms">
            {c.perms.map((p) => (
              <li class="perm" id={`${slug(c.name)}--${slug(p.action)}`} data-tier={p.tier ?? ''} data-text={`${c.name} ${p.action} ${p.ms} ${p.note ?? ''}`.toLowerCase()}>
                <div class="ph">
                  <h3>{p.action}</h3>
                  {p.tier === 'never' && <span class="badge never">Never by default</span>}
                  {p.tier === 'high' && <span class="badge high">High impact</span>}
                  {p.live && <span class="badge new" title="In a live tenant, not yet documented on Microsoft Learn">New</span>}
                </div>
                <p class="ms"><span class="lbl">{p.live ? 'Microsoft (via Graph)' : 'Microsoft'}</span>{p.ms}</p>
                {p.note && <p class="note"><span class="lbl">In practice</span>{p.note}</p>}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </section>
      ))}
      <p id="empty" class="empty" hidden>No permissions match that filter.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="prose more">
      <h2>Further reading</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={sourceUrl}>Create a custom role in Intune</a>, Microsoft Learn</li>
        <li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/fundamentals/role-based-access-control/ref-built-in-roles">Built-in role permissions for Microsoft Intune</a>, Microsoft Learn</li>
        <li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/intune-rbac-resourceoperation-list?view=graph-rest-beta">List resourceOperations (Microsoft Graph beta)</a>, Microsoft Learn</li>
        <li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/device-management/deployments/overview">Deployment plans and deployments overview</a>, Microsoft Learn</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var q = document.getElementById('q');
    var risky = document.getElementById('risky');
    var count = document.getElementById('count');
    var empty = document.getElementById('empty');
    var perms = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.perm'));
    var cats = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.cat'));
    function apply() {
      var term = q.value.trim().toLowerCase();
      var onlyRisky = risky.checked;
      var shown = 0;
      perms.forEach(function (el) {
        var ok = (!term || el.getAttribute('data-text').indexOf(term) !== -1) && (!onlyRisky || el.getAttribute('data-tier'));
        el.hidden = !ok;
        if (ok) shown++;
      });
      cats.forEach(function (sec) {
        var any = sec.querySelector('.perm:not([hidden])');
        sec.hidden = !any;
        var link = document.querySelector('[data-cat-link="' + sec.getAttribute('data-cat') + '"]');
        if (link) link.hidden = !any;
      });
      count.textContent = shown + (shown === 1 ? ' permission' : ' permissions');
      empty.hidden = shown !== 0;
    }
    q.addEventListener('input', apply);
    risky.addEventListener('change', apply);
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .head { background: var(--paper-2); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); border-top: 6px solid var(--accent); padding: 40px 0 40px; }
  .crumbs { display: flex; gap: 8px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); }
  .crumbs a { color: var(--muted); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5vw, 3.2rem); line-height: 1.06; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 16px 0 14px; }
  .lead { margin: 0; max-width: 64ch; font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .facts { margin: 16px 0 0; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--muted); }
  .facts a { color: var(--muted); }
  .body { padding-top: 40px; }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .intro, .check, .more { max-width: 72ch; }
  .check, .more { margin-top: 48px; }

  .badge {
    display: inline-block; white-space: nowrap; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 999px; vertical-align: 2px;
  }
  .badge.never { background: #b3001b; color: #fff; }
  .badge.high { background: #f2b544; color: #3a2600; }
  .badge.new { background: transparent; color: var(--accent); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--accent); }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .badge.never { background: #ff6b6b; color: #1a0000; } }

  .never-box { margin-top: 48px; padding: 28px; border: 2px solid #b3001b; border-radius: 14px; background: var(--paper); }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .never-box { border-color: #ff6b6b; } }
  .never-box h2 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 1.4rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .never-box > p { margin: 0 0 16px; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .never-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .never-list li { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 10px; align-items: baseline; font-size: 16px; }
  .nc { font-weight: 700; min-width: 15ch; }
  .never-list a { padding: 2px 0; }
  .never-list a:not(:last-child)::after { content: ','; color: var(--muted); }

  .tools {
    position: sticky; top: 64px; z-index: 3; margin-top: 48px; padding: 16px 0 14px; background: var(--paper);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px 18px;
  }
  .tools > label:first-child { position: absolute; left: -9999px; }
  .tools input[type='search'] {
    flex: 1 1 280px; min-height: 48px; padding: 0 14px; font: inherit; font-size: 17px; color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper); border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px;
  }
  .tools input[type='search']:focus { outline: none; border-color: var(--accent); }
  .chk { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; min-height: 44px; font-size: 15px; }
  .chk input { width: 20px; height: 20px; accent-color: var(--accent); }
  .count { margin: 0; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }

  .index { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 8px; margin: 20px 0 8px; }
  .index a {
    font-size: 14px; padding: 6px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .index a:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--ink); }

  .cat { margin-top: 44px; scroll-margin-top: 150px; }
  .cat h2 { font-size: 1.55rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em; margin: 0 0 6px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 3px solid var(--accent); }
  .sum { margin: 10px 0 0; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 72ch; }
  .perms { list-style: none; margin: 16px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .perm { padding: 16px 18px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--paper); scroll-margin-top: 150px; }
  .perm:target { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--accent); }
  .ph { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 12px; align-items: center; }
  .perm h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.35; }
  .perm p { margin: 8px 0 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 80ch; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .ms { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .lbl {
    display: inline-block; margin-right: 8px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .note .lbl { color: var(--accent); }
  .empty { margin-top: 32px; color: var(--muted); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .tools { position: static; }
    .cat, .perm { scroll-margin-top: 72px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .never-box { padding: 20px; }
    .nc { min-width: 0; width: 100%; }
  }
</style>
